# Cloudflare Pages redirects — copied verbatim into dist/ by Astro.
#
# Canonical host: www.toolsai.club
#
# The site answers on two names, and only one of them may serve content. If both
# https://toolsai.club/ and https://www.toolsai.club/ return 200 with the same page, every URL exists
# twice, the canonical tag and the host's own behaviour disagree, and a search engine is free to pick
# either - which is the arrangement that splits a page's signals between two addresses. The canonical
# constant in src/consts.ts names the www form; this file is what makes the other form stop answering.
#
# 301, not 302: the choice is permanent and should be cached as such.
#
# The splat carries the path through, so a deep link keeps its destination instead of landing on the
# homepage - the failure mode of a redirect written without one.
#
# Query strings: Cloudflare Pages forwards the query string to the destination when the target does not
# declare one of its own. That is the documented behaviour and it is NOT verified here - this repository
# has no deployed environment, and the command that added this rule forbade deploying. Check it with a
# real request the first time the site is live (see the launch checklist).
#
# Order matters: the first matching rule wins. There is one rule and no catch-all, deliberately - a
# catch-all would also capture the domain this site will use.
#
# The previous project's two rules were removed on 2026-10-26. They named the domain that project used,
# which this project does not own, so they could never fire here - and leaving them in the file would
# suggest the redirect had been configured when it had not.
https://toolsai.club/* https://www.toolsai.club/:splat 301
